{
 "mouth_keepout": {
  "what": "Ellipse on the FRONT surface (rest space, front projection x,y; applies where z>0.15) that no wearable may enter.",
  "centre_xy": [
   0.0,
   0.651
  ],
  "radii_xy": [
   0.15,
   0.1
  ],
  "test": "((x-0)/0.15)^2 + ((y-0.651)/0.10)^2 < 1  and z > 0.15  => inside",
  "y_range_at_x0": [
   0.551,
   0.751
  ],
  "source": "Shaders.metal fsSoftMatte mouth: drawn at x=0, y=0.665 (DineGeometry.mouthRest = (0,0.665,z_surface~0.52)); at mouthOpen=1 (largest: eating chomp 0.25+0.75m reaches 1.0; yawn/snore 0.95*m) half-width 0.088, up 0.066/1.45=0.0455, down 0.066/0.9=0.0733 => open mouth spans y 0.5917..0.7105. keep-out = that D-shape + 0.04 margin, bounded by this ellipse.",
  "food_lands": "tossed food/sip targets DineGeometry.mouthRest (0,0.665,z~0.52); the toss/straw paths come from the front/above toward that point."
 },
 "units": "Jelly REST space = world units (BobForm; floor y=0, crown y=1.3458, +z = face)",
 "file_format": "OBJ: v x y z r g b ao w (rgb LINEAR vertex colour, ao 0.6..1 baked from distance to body, w=0 RoomMaterial.plain), vn, o <part>, f a//a b//b c//c (CCW). One <id>.json sidecar each.",
 "palette_srgb": {
  "cream": "#F7F0E0",
  "ink": "#4D331F",
  "sky": "#6EB3D1",
  "pink": "#E98AA4",
  "honey": "#F9CC59",
  "mint": "#9FD9B0",
  "lavender": "#B9A3E6",
  "coral": "#F58B6E"
 },
 "anchor_conventions": {
  "head_top": "anchor_rest=(0,1.3458,0) = crown of the egg (BobForm.top). Mesh vertices are REST-space offsets from the anchor: restPos = anchor_rest + v. Axes = body rest axes (y up, +z face, x = Jelly's right-of-screen when facing camera). Carry: world = bodyPointWorld(restPos) per vertex (same maths as EyeMaskModel).",
  "face": "anchor_rest = front surface at (0, eyeY=0.82), z=0.5052. Rest-space offsets, same carry as head_top. Lens/rim centres sit on frontSurface(+-eyeX=0.215, 0.82) pushed 0.050 along the body normal (>= the mask's 0.014 pad), so eye beads (eyeHalfW .0532 x eyeHalfH .0623) are never touched.",
  "neck": "anchor_rest = front surface at (0, 0.47), z=0.5055 ('neck' = the chest just under the mouth: there is no neck on an egg). Rest-space offsets, same carry.",
  "chest": "anchor_rest = front surface at (0, 0.355), z=0.4683 (lower belly, below the mouth keep-out zone). Rest-space offsets, same carry.",
  "wrist": "NOT rest space. Mesh is in the ARM-LOCAL frame (origin = arm tip centre B; +y = unit(A-B) toward the shoulder; +x outward = cross(y,+z_body); +z = body forward), authored for the +x arm. restPos(rest pose) = anchor_rest + R*v with R columns in local_frame.rest_matrix_columns; for a posed arm build the same frame from the posed capsule (A,B) and scale by r2/0.15. Mirror x (flip winding) for the -x arm.",
  "number": "Digit meshes: unit height, centred on their box, +z out of the plate, depth ~0.06. Place at bib.number_anchor_rest with the plate normal (bib.number_normal), scale by bib.number_height (0.24). Colours are baked cream: replace vertex colours to tint (team colour deep shade).",
  "carry_verified": "Verified in SleepMask.swift: EyeMaskModel.Carry(centroid, rotation, squash, restCentroid) is applied PER VERTEX: world = centroid + R * ((rest - restCentroid) * (sxz, sy, sxz)). Same for every rest-space piece here.",
  "back": "NEW (batch 2). anchor_rest=(0,0.55,-0.5172) = back surface of the egg at y=0.55 (B.egg_point(0.55, 270deg)). Rest-space offsets (x right-of-screen when facing the camera, y up, +z = face, so the back is z<0); restPos = anchor_rest + v. Same per-vertex Carry as head_top. Back items never have vertices at z>0.15 except none; their vertices are free-hanging (cape, backpack).",
  "waist": "NEW (batch 2). anchor_rest=(0,0.28,0) = on-axis point at belly-waist height (like head_top, on the body axis, not on the surface). Rest-space offsets; a full ring around the egg: bind each vertex to egg param (y,phi) + horizontal-outward offset (skirt flares outward and down from y~0.27).",
  "face_note_batch2": "goggles_aviator uses the standard 'face' anchor although it sits on the forehead (y 0.99..1.15); offsets are rest-space so nothing changes. Monocle: ring around the +x eye bead; mirror x for the other eye."
 },
